
> ...the storm booming without in solemn swells; I began to be sensible of
> strange feelings. I felt a melting in me. No more my splintered heart and
> maddened hand were turned against the wolfish world...

---

and maddened hand is a notekeeping system for neovim.

== Syntax

While it isn't in any way necessary, I'd encourage users to avoid using
newlines for any purpose other than delimiting the end of a given "item". The
plugin will configure neovim to soft-wrap and soft-indent long lines in a way
which is visually pleasant and which should be easy to navigate in the usual
vim fashion.

=== Checklists

A checklist might look something like:

  - [ ] unchecked item
  - [ ] another such
  - [x] checked item
    - [ ] checked subitem
    - [ ] unchecked subitem
      - [x] checked subsubitem
  - [ ] yet another top-level unchecked item

Each item should be written entirely on a single line. The plugin will ensure
that line contents are word-wrapped and indented in a pleasant fashion.

=== Links

A link from a mh file to FooBar.mh would be written like:

  :FooBar

Such a link can be inserted anywhere that text might otherwise go, such as:

  - [ ] update :FooBar process doc

